Propagate update classification to inline accessors

Under separation checking, an inline method that mutates state through a
private member generates a synthetic accessor (inline$x_= or a call
forwarder) that is not classified as an update method, so the mutation
fails the exclusivity check inside the accessor. Give the accessor the
Mutable flag when the accessed symbol is an update method, or when it is
a mutable field and the accessor is its setter.

Proscala-Patch: inlineupdate
